      "item": "dart_has_doc_comment",
      "reviewed": true,
      "intent": "Detect whether a Dart doc comment (/// line comment or /** */ block comment) is attached to a declaration. Tracked items are inner signature nodes, so climb through the declaration wrapper nodes before inspecting preceding siblings. Treat tree-sitter-dart's documentation_comment node kind as a doc comment, and skip annotation siblings such as @override.",
      "source_span": [
        36,
        74
      ],
      "tree_path": "fn.dart_has_doc_comment",
      "source_hash": "sha256:0495ba8328a4417c16e2b32ddc21055bcf951bb76b1c8ec2696c0ffe98dc9264",
      "source_anchor": "fn dart_has_doc_comment(node: &Node, source: &str) -> bool {"
    },
    {
      "item": "CONFIG",
      "reviewed": true,
      "intent": "Define the Dart language configuration for tree_path resolution: register the tree-sitter-dart grammar, .dart extension, and kind mappings for fn (function_signature), class, mixin, extension, extension_type, enum, getter, setter, and the constructor variants. Use class_body, extension_body, and enum_body for container descent, and wire the custom dart_node_name and dart_has_doc_comment callbacks. Declare member_declaration, method_signature, declaration, method_declaration, function_declaration, getter_declaration, and setter_declaration as transparent wrapper kinds so resolve_segments can see through declaration wrappers to inner signature nodes.",
